#!/usr/bin/env Rscript

# =============================================================================
# CORRECTED COMBINED DEG, VOLCANO, TABLE 1, AND GO/KEGG ANALYSIS
# =============================================================================
# Changes in this version:
# - sex-adjusted edgeR results are the manuscript-facing DEG and enrichment results;
# - the unadjusted model is retained only as an optional comparison controlled by
#   run_unadjusted_comparison, and optional unadjusted enrichment is controlled
#   separately by include_unadjusted_enrichment_comparison;
# - all DEG, GO/KEGG, and multiple-testing significance thresholds reported for
#   the manuscript are FDR/BH-adjusted P < 0.01;
# - Table 1 is rebuilt entirely from sex-adjusted DEGs, including contrast-specific
#   unique DEGs and total/up/down mouse-ortholog counts and percentages;
# - two-sided Fisher tests compare mouse-ortholog proportions between upregulated
#   and downregulated DEGs in each contrast, followed by BH correction;
# - explicit manuscript DEG-count summaries distinguish DEG calls, distinct DEGs,
#   contrast-specific unique DEGs, multi-contrast DEGs, and warm-cold-boundary DEGs;
# - Ensembl biomaRt and KEGG queries use retry logic; complete Ensembl query failure
#   stops the analysis, while KEGG query failure is explicitly recorded in outputs;
# - the tested-gene sets from the sex-adjusted and unadjusted models are verified
#   to be identical whenever the unadjusted comparison is run;
# - the existing volcano styling, enrichment audit trail, explicit mapped universe,
#   automatic mouse-identifier selection, RDS output, and sessionInfo() are retained.
#
# ASSUMPTION -- "unique DEG": a contrast-specific unique DEG is significant at
# FDR < 0.01 in exactly one of the six sex-adjusted contrasts. "Distinct DEGs"
# instead means the union of all genes significant in at least one contrast.
#
# ASSUMPTION -- 1:1 orthologs: a non-empty Target_gene is counted as an assigned
# 1:1 mouse ortholog only if Target_gene contains exclusively validated 1:1 mouse
# ortholog assignments. The script prints a runtime warning about this assumption.
# =============================================================================

